# Copy this file to .env and fill in the key. .env is gitignored.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Use a **Secret key (server)** from the Petify Console (Integration → API &
# SDK → Create New API Key). The example's demo backend registers, identifies
# and verifies pets, which a Client key may not do. It runs against the
# production backend the console issues keys for: a registration here is a real
# pet in your account (you can delete it from "See all" on the home screen).
#
# Note for your own app: the key is inlined into the JS bundle at build time,
# which is fine for a sample you run locally and wrong for something you ship.
# A shipping app holds a Client key (app); the Secret key stays on your server.
PETIFY_API_KEY=
